\par\b\fs28 A4. Movement\b0\fs24\par


\par What is unmasked? Forgetting the Rock in abundance \u8212? receiving that turns into possessing \u8212? and the treacherous idolatry that does not reject God but makes Him practically unnecessary; visible in the hard hand toward the neighbour (Matt. 18).\par


\par What frame does the text put in its place? The unchanging Rock who gives and heals; teshuvah as looking again at Him, and \u8220?from Me is your fruit found.\u8221?\par


\par What concrete response and formation follow? Listen (ha'azinu); return with words (Hosea); rend your heart, not your garments (Joel); and let the received forgiveness open the hand toward the other (Matt. 18).\par


\par \b Core sentence:\b0  The Rock does not change; the heart forgets \u8212? return, and let the grace you received open the hand you stretch out to your brother.\par


\par \b Horizon (ground, not the week's theme):\b0  \u8220?I kill and I make alive, I heal\u8221? (32:39) and \u8220?from Me your fruit\u8221? (Hos. 14:8) \u8212? the restoration comes from the Rock, not from our achievement.\par


